      "settlement": "Nellvaris",
      "settlementKey": "falthrakar:Nellvaris",
      "description": "Katy Storybell is a careful, warm, slightly anxious schoolteacher who believes education is one of the last honest tools civilization has left. As a Half-Elf shaped by Nebyrr’s influence toward lineage, civic order, and cultural bridging, she teaches children practical literacy, local history, safety skills, moral reasoning, and the expectations of settlement life. She loves her students deeply, but shrinking class sizes and limited teaching materials make her quietly worry that she is preparing them for a world she herself is too cautious to face.",
      "settlementAndAncestryTexture": "Nellvaris is a Capital City in Falthrakar, under Diarchy, with elevated danger, Farming, Beach and grass with water, Partial forest terrain. Local records favor Altruistic, Lawful, Cooperative, Honorable civic habits; common communities include Human, Halfling — Lightfoot Halfling, Halfling — Stout Halfling, Kender, Kithkin. Half-Elf reads through the Half-Elf (choose an Elf Bloodline) entry of the race compendium, within Humans, Near-Humans, and Mixed Heritage, marked by Nebyrr. Half-elves are dual-natured beings born of human and elven lineage, often balancing ambition with longevity. They tend to struggle with identity but excel at diplomacy, adaptability, and bridging cultures. Table cues: +2 Charisma, +1 to Two Other Ability Scores, Darkvision, Fey Ancestry; starting tendency Neutral - Lawful - Cooperative - Neutral.",
      "rumors": [
        "Katy Storybell knows why an ichor ledger changed hands last Valkhaday.",
        "Katy Storybell has a contact in Yltharien who will deny everything."
      ],
      "plotHooks": [
